Subject: [S] Equivalent Number of Parameters
Message-ID: <199906020652.AA00012@takezawa.affrc.go.jp>

E-mail: s-news at wubios.wustl.edu

Hi!

   I figured out the problem below by myself.

>   My question is on "Equivalent Number of Parameters" which
>is one of the outputs from "loess()". My understanding is that
>this value is summation of squared elements of Hat matrix.
>I calculated this value using its definition. The program
>I used and results are below. It shows that the value from
>"loess()" is 6.2, and the value form Hat matrix is 6.950691.
>I am wondering if this is because this data is ill-conditioned.

   If a user need the exact value of "Equivalent Number of
Parameters", you should specify ' statistics="exact" ' in
loess.control(). It will result in the same value as the one
which is obtained using its definition, though computational
time gets longer.
   My concern is that loess() gives approximated value
of "Equivalent Number of Parameters" by default, so that 
some people may take this value as the exact one and use it for
estimation of confidence intervals for example. This might
lead to dangerous outcome. I would suggest that loess()
should not display approximated "Equivalent Number of 
Parameters" by default, and specification in loess.control()
should be required if a user need an approximated value or
an exact value of "Equivalent Number of Parameters".

