I sent out a message yesterday with the following question:

> Under Splus5 Release 3 on Solaris I have been getting an error message
> complaining about "too many open files," even though I am not
> explicitly opening any files at all.  Has anyone else seen this
> problem and know what's going on or whether there is a workaround?
> 
> I'm sorry to be so vague but I haven't been able to narrow the problem
> down to a specific function or to write a simple piece of code that
> reproduces the error.  The problem appears to happen when I iterate
> over a large number of Splus objects, "getting" each one in turn.
> (But this is not a sufficient condition.)
> 

Thanks to Douglas Bates, Phil Spector, Martin, and Bill Dunlap of
MathSoft for responding.  Bill Dunlap's suggestion was to call

  mmap.control(.Machine$integer.max)

and this works.

Apparently Splus automatically memory-maps objects over a certain
threshold---50KB by default---and this call increases that threshold.
The mmap.control function is documented in the Release Notes under
"Backward Compatibility Issues."
