Message-ID: <Pine.GSO.4.10.9906041741460.4843-100000@compstat.wharton.upenn.edu>

Simply speaking, S+ is superior for explortory data analysis and Matlab is
for serious calculation and simulation. 

One feature of Matlab is that you can compile the script to binary to run
faster. (It is alreay much faster than SPLUS.) Even more, it comes with C
math library (matlab/compiler) so each M-file can be translated to
standalone C/C++ program and linked against the library. This is one thing
SPLUS definitely lacks.

Also, if you only want to do simulation -- SPLUS program can be used in
SAS/IML with little modification. SAS is known to be great to handle
large dataset. SAS/IML and SPLUS have similar grammar.

Hope it helps.

