Subject: [S] .S.chapters in Splus 5.1
Message-ID: <v03130304b384a18ab0f7@[128.115.153.6]>

If this has previously been mentioned on snews, I apologize for the
duplication. But I don'r recalls seeing it.

For those who are not aware, Splus 5.1 under unix has a new feature for
attaching chapters at startup time. If a file named .S.chapters exists (in
certain locations), all chapters listed in that file will be attached at
startup time.

If there are blank lines in this file, Splus will attempt to attach a
chapter whose name is "", resulting in an error message. Since it's pretty
easy to accidentally add blank lines to a file, it is unfortunate that the
function standardChapters() does not remove blanks from its list of
chapters to attach.

