Subject: [S] Summary: statistical question: ROC curves
Message-ID: <3766375D.C5120025@HRZ.Uni-Dortmund.DE>

Hallo,

I like to thank all persons who responded to my email concerning the
comparison of ROC curves.

> I apologize, this is more a statistical question than a question about S-PLUS.
>
> Are there papers or tables which can be used to plan the number of cases 
> required to compare the
>areas under two ROC curves ?
>
> I like to use the nonparametric approach proposed in:
> deLong, E.R., deLong, D.M., Clarke-Pearson, D.L. (1988).
>  Comparing the Areas Under Two or More Correlated Receiver
> Operating Characteristic Curves:
>  A Nonparametric Approach. Biometrics, 44, 837-845.

Many people helped me and I like to give a short summary.
------------------------------
Beth Atkinson: Check out the Mayo Biostatistics webpage at
  www.mayo.edu/hsr/biostat.html
with helpful S-Plus functions.
------------------------------
Charles C. Berry send very helpful informations about
S-Plus functions to simulate the power and
sample sizes considerations.
------------------------------
L. Y. Hin told me to check:
Hanley JA, and McNeil BJ Radiology 1982;143:29-36
Hanley JA, and McNeil BJ Radiology 1983;148:839-843.
----------------------------------------------

Recently I found the interesting paper
  Venkatraman, E.S. and Begg, C.B. (1996).
  Distribution-free procedure for comparing ROC curves.
  Biometrika 83, pp. 835-848.
These authors propose a new statistical method and
compare their method with the deLong et al. method.
In this paper there are some valuable tables concerning
power analysis and sample size determination for both
methods.

Thank you again,

Andreas Christmann
