Hi.

Details:

Version : 3.4
OS: IBM RS/6000, AIX 3.2.5

The following code is being used to compute a Choleski decomposition
of a matrix created in SAS. The SAS program and this S program are
working interactively.

The matrix is the covariance matrix resulting from a regression
procedure, and is dumped into the file named 'outdata'. Control
is then passed to S-Plus from within SAS. S-Plus exports the
Choleski decomposition to the file 'newData'.

The problem is that S-Plus returns control to SAS before the file
is fully created. I solved the problem by writing a SAS macro that
simply loops until the file exists, but I'm wondering if there
is a better way.

Specifically, can I somehow force S to maintain control until
the file is complete?

data <- scan ("outdata", list (row=0, col=0, datum=0))
N    <- max (data$col)
mat  <- matrix (data$datum, ncol=N, byrow=T)
out  <- chol (mat)
out  <- cbind (row=1:N, col=rep (1:N, rep (N,N)), datum=as.vector (out))

write.table (out, file="newData", sep="\t")

Thanks.

