Subject: [S] Re: your mail
Message-ID: <v03102811b38d8ecf42ed@[199.4.81.92]>

The correct solution follows. Thanks to all who responded,
and in particular to Bill Dunlap for pointing me
in the right direction.

I had been using the SAS statements

" X 'Splus BATCH infile outfile' ; "
" %wait (filename) ; " /* A macro that waits until the file exists. */

instead of

" X 'Splus < infile > outfile' ; "

Andrzej Galecki correctly points out that IML can be used to
find a Choleski decomposition, but the expense of purchasing
IML was what prompted me to look for other solutions.

Thanks again.

--Charles.

